/P 374 0 R
/T (This study contributes new evidence base on how social media safety features are experienced and used in everyday practice. Drawing on insights from the co-design workshops and expert consultations, we identify six key recommendations aimed at strengthening both the design and governance of platform safety systems. These recommendations address areas such as improving transparency in reporting processes, introducing preventative design measures that reduce opportunities for abuse, making safety tools easier to discover and use, and strengthening accountability in how platforms respond to harm.)
/E (This study contributes new evidence base on how social media safety features are experienced and used in everyday practice. Drawing on insights from the co-design workshops and expert consultations, we identify six key recommendations aimed at strengthening both the design and governance of platform safety systems. These recommendations address areas such as improving transparency in reporting processes, introducing preventative design measures that reduce opportunities for abuse, making safety tools easier to discover and use, and strengthening accountability in how platforms respond to harm.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [10]
>>
