/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 377 0 R
/T (This report contributes new and in-depth evidence drawn from a substantial program of co-design workshops with adult women and gender-diverse social media users across Australia, including strong representation from culturally and linguistically diverse communities. The scale of participation exceeds many existing qualitative studies in this domain, enabling a broader range of scenarios, perspectives, and safety concerns to be surfaced. Importantly, the study also integrates expert workshops involving professionals in platform safety, digital policy, moderation, and technology governance. This dual-perspective approach allows for both user-generated proposals and critical examination of feasibility, proportionality, governance implications, and unintended consequences.)
/E (This report contributes new and in-depth evidence drawn from a substantial program of co-design workshops with adult women and gender-diverse social media users across Australia, including strong representation from culturally and linguistically diverse communities. The scale of participation exceeds many existing qualitative studies in this domain, enabling a broader range of scenarios, perspectives, and safety concerns to be surfaced. Importantly, the study also integrates expert workshops involving professionals in platform safety, digital policy, moderation, and technology governance. This dual-perspective approach allows for both user-generated proposals and critical examination of feasibility, proportionality, governance implications, and unintended consequences.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
