/T (Participants also expressed uncertainty about whether screenshots alone would be considered trustworthy or sufficient, particularly if they needed to escalate a case to the platform, the Australian eSafety Commissioner, or police. As a result, current approaches felt fragile, time-consuming, and dependent on users remembering to document incidents themselves.)
/E (Participants also expressed uncertainty about whether screenshots alone would be considered trustworthy or sufficient, particularly if they needed to escalate a case to the platform, the Australian eSafety Commissioner, or police. As a result, current approaches felt fragile, time-consuming, and dependent on users remembering to document incidents themselves.)
