/T (To reduce these risks, participants suggested adding preventative friction during the sharing process itself. Ideas included warning screens before sending intimate media, blur-by-default previews for the recipient, timers or one-time viewing options, and prompts that ask for confirmation or consent before content is posted or forwarded. Others suggested requiring permission before downloading or resharing sensitive images, or automatically limiting how widely such content can be distributed. These measures were framed as small interruptions that create space to reflect, rather than hard restrictions that block communication entirely.)
