/T (Some participants expressed the stress and uncertainty of being impersonated online. When someone created a look-alike profile using their name or photos, the original person often struggled to prove impersonation. Participants said this made reporting impersonating accounts feel slow and frustrating, as platforms appeared to rely on profile photos or basic information that could easily be copied. As a result, the burden of proof often fell on the victim rather than the impersonator.)
