/T (Participants frequently discussed the potential role of artificial intelligence and behavioural analysis in identifying patterns of abuse before harm escalates. Many users described online abuse as ongoing and patterned rather than isolated incidents. For example, harassment may involve repeated messages, the creation of multiple accounts after being blocked, persistent commenting across posts, or the circulation of explicit or fabricated images over time. Because of this, participants expected platforms to look beyond individual pieces of content and recognise behavioural patterns that signal possible abuse.)
/E (Participants frequently discussed the potential role of artificial intelligence and behavioural analysis in identifying patterns of abuse before harm escalates. Many users described online abuse as ongoing and patterned rather than isolated incidents. For example, harassment may involve repeated messages, the creation of multiple accounts after being blocked, persistent commenting across posts, or the circulation of explicit or fabricated images over time. Because of this, participants expected platforms to look beyond individual pieces of content and recognise behavioural patterns that signal possible abuse.)
/Pg 73 0 R
/K [6]
