/Title (A recurring frustration across workshops was the lack of visibility once a report was submitted. Participants described reporting harmful posts or accounts and then hearing nothing back, sometimes for days or weeks. Without updates, it was unclear whether the report had been received, reviewed, or acted upon. Several participants also noted that they did not know whether a dashboard or dedicated space even existed to check on the status of their reports. This uncertainty left people feeling ignored, unsupported, or forced to repeatedly report the same issue or ask friends to help escalate it.)
