7468 0 obj
<<
/Title (Experts supported timely escalation pathways for high-risk cases but emphasised the need for clear severity triage and structured human oversight. They cautioned that without careful scoping and coordination with external authorities, such mechanisms could create unrealistic expectations or operational strain.)
/Dest [46 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7442 0 R
/Next 7490 0 R
>>
endobj
7469 0 obj
<<
/Title (Workshop Findings: Theme 2 Content Controls)
/Dest [47 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7442 0 R
/Prev 7490 0 R
>>
endobj
7470 0 obj
<<
/Title (Providing direct access to human moderators or external authorities can improve user reassurance and support documentation for potential legal action. At the same time, experts noted risks including reports being escalated to law enforcement prematurely or without sufficient evidence, the potential for malicious misuse of escalation pathways, and users developing expectations that platforms can guarantee an immediate police response. Clear criteria and safeguards would therefore be necessary to prevent misuse and ensure escalation pathways function as intended.)
/Dest [47 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7443 0 R
>>
endobj
7471 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [48 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7375 0 R
/Prev 7445 0 R
/Next 7491 0 R
>>
endobj
